summary_en.reading_guide:
must_read (deep read):
- Key sections: Introduction (motivation + 3 limitations), System & Adversary Model (retrieval/write-back loop + black-box constraints), and the method section detailing “distribution estimation + entropy-guided query selection + iterative updates” (candidate construction, update rule, stopping/budget).
- Key figures/tables: Figure 1 (agent memory workflow and attack insertion point), main comparison tables (ASR across agents/LLMs/defenses), ablation tables (removing distribution estimation or entropy strategy), and oracle results (upper bound and gap).
- Innovation checklist: (i) highlighting and validating the role of memory data distribution, (ii) entropy/information-gain driven adaptive querying, (iii) systematic evaluation tailored to agent settings (multi-turn, planning, persistent memory) beyond standalone RAG.

skim (quick read):
- Read Introduction + Threat Model to align assumptions;
- Jump to the method overview/flow to grasp the iterative loop and entropy intuition;
- Read main results vs. baselines/defenses;
- Skim ablations to confirm distribution estimation is the main contributor.
